alled embers and it  works a little differently yeah so when  you die which we did a lot during our  time the game as most people do you stop  being what they're calling the kindled  one this whole game the story revolves  around you know these people coming back  to reclaim the ember or something  similar but um when you awake at the  bonfire you have a little less max hit  points but also you don't have your emer  anymore so there is there are items that  you find that it's called embers and you  can either kill a boss to have your  ember restored as it says or use the  ember which will fill your help up all  the way but you can only use one her  life so they're probably you know  they're going to be more important as  you play through the game it also looked  like something you could use as a last  resort so if you run out of all your SS  flasks and you're almost done with the  boss you can use an ember to kind of  fill up your health just to get those  last few hits and kind of finish it up  another new thing that we found is more  combat variety looks like real  comparable to previous games in the dark  souls series it's giving you more  opportunities outside of your standard  sword and shield yeah so those were  largely focused around those kind of  slow methodical fights Dark Souls 1 and  2 but now even more so than in Dark  Souls 2 which kind of open it up you can  really just tailor to your place though  you know we were in the beta when you  and I played a few months ago we were  kind of both trying out the dual  wielding we also you know tried the  typical sword and shield with the night  I was the warrior which is kind of a new  barbarian in the demo we played and the  big axe yeah and I was pretty much just  do a willing to act the whole time just  relying on my dodge and upping my  endurance whenever I could when I was  leveling up so it definitely seems like  they are kind of using blood-borne as  you know the jumping off point to  introduce a little 